Package: kmod-gpio-button-hotplug
Version: 6.6.79-r5
Depends: kernel (=6.6.79~614b8d7b217994022d93abee2d7530a6-r1)
Source: feeds/base/kernel/gpio-button-hotplug
SourceName: gpio-button-hotplug
License: GPL-2.0
Section: kernel
SourceDateEpoch: 1771803568
Architecture: aarch64_cortex-a53
Installed-Size: 30720
Filename: kmod-gpio-button-hotplug_6.6.79-r5_aarch64_cortex-a53.ipk
Size: 6906
SHA256sum: 94ea4480a70bfb36ff63c3e96d514178f82c5dec11f0bf4cb304f89752a1b960
Description:  This is a replacement for the following in-kernel drivers:
 1) gpio_keys (KEYBOARD_GPIO)
 2) gpio_keys_polled (KEYBOARD_GPIO_POLLED)
 
 Instead of generating input events (like in-kernel drivers do) it generates
 uevent-s and broadcasts them. This allows disabling input subsystem which is
 an overkill for OpenWrt simple needs.

